From: Mihawk <163614687+mihawk-99@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] d3d9: A window message filter skips a window that was never
 hooked

A D3D9 Reset from fullscreen to fullscreen that names a new device window
(D3DPRESENT_PARAMETERS.hDeviceWindow) makes it the swapchain's window and
then builds a D3D9WindowMessageFilter for it. Only the window the
swapchain entered fullscreen with was hooked, so g_windowProcMap has no
entry for the new one, and the filter dereferenced the map's end(): a
read at 0x19 through a null node, a crash. A window that was never hooked
has no message filter to set or restore: skip it.

From PS5_MihawkOS (platform/dxvk/patches/0006), zlib licence as DXVK.
---
 src/d3d9/d3d9_window.cpp | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/d3d9/d3d9_window.cpp b/src/d3d9/d3d9_window.cpp
index 4e44a8d..937be76 100644
--- a/src/d3d9/d3d9_window.cpp
+++ b/src/d3d9/d3d9_window.cpp
@@ -22,13 +22,16 @@ namespace dxvk
     : m_window(window) {
     std::lock_guard lock(g_windowProcMapMutex);
     auto it = g_windowProcMap.find(m_window);
-    m_filter = std::exchange(it->second.filter, filter);
+    // a Reset can name a device window that was never hooked: nothing to filter then
+    if (it != g_windowProcMap.end())
+      m_filter = std::exchange(it->second.filter, filter);
   }
 
   D3D9WindowMessageFilter::~D3D9WindowMessageFilter() {
     std::lock_guard lock(g_windowProcMapMutex);
     auto it = g_windowProcMap.find(m_window);
-    it->second.filter = m_filter;
+    if (it != g_windowProcMap.end())
+      it->second.filter = m_filter;
   }
 
   LRESULT CALLBACK D3D9WindowProc(HWND window, UINT message, WPARAM wparam, LPARAM lparam) {
